text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures able to block target creature this turn do so.', 'Blaze deals X damage to any target.', 'Borrowing the East Wind deals X damage to each creature with horsemanship and each player.', 'Burning Fields deals 5 damage to target opponent or planeswalker.', "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nCreatures you control get +2/+2 until end of turn.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nDestroy target attacking creature.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt to you this turn by attacking creatures.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nReturn target attacking creature to its owner's hand.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nUntap all creatures you control.", 'Counter target creature or sorcery spell.', 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Counter target sorcery spell.', "Creatures and lands target opponent controls don't untap during their next untap step.", 'Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Creatures you control have horsemanship. (They can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", 'Desert Sandstorm deals 1 damage to each creature.', 'Destroy all creatures target opponent controls. Draw a card for each creature destroyed this way.', 'Destroy all lands.', 'Destroy all tapped creatures.', 'Destroy target creature with horsemanship.', 'Destroy target creature. Its owner gains 4 life.', 'Destroy target land.', 'Destroy target nonblack creature.', 'Destroy target nonblack creature. You gain 3 life.', 'Destroy target tapped creature.', 'Draw a card for each tapped creature target opponent controls.', 'Draw four cards, then discard three cards at random.', 'Draw three cards.', 'Famine deals 3 damage to each creature and each player.', 'Fire Ambush deals 3 damage to any target.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Haste', "Haste; horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nZuo Ci, the Mocking Sage can't be blocked by creatures with horsemanship.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nEach creature you control can't be blocked by more than one creature.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nLiu Bei, Lord of Shu gets +2/+2 as long as you control a permanent named Guan Yu, Sainted Warrior or a permanent named Zhang Fei, Fierce Warrior.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nSacrifice Xiahou Dun, the One-Eyed: Return target black card from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhen Cao Ren, Wei Commander enters the battlefield, you lose 3 life.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhen Guan Yu, Sainted Warrior is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may shuffle Guan Yu into your library.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhen Sun Ce, Young Conquerer enters the battlefield, you may return target creature to its owner's hand.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhen Wu Scout enters the battlefield, look at target opponent's hand.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhenever Lu Xun, Scholar General deals damage to an opponent, you may draw a card.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhenever Ma Chao, Western Warrior attacks alone, it can't be blocked this combat.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhenever Wei Night Raiders deals damage to an opponent, that player discards a card.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhenever Zhang He, Wei General attacks, each other creature you control gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nWhenever Zhao Zilong, Tiger General blocks, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nYellow Scarves Cavalry can't block.", "Horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)\\nYellow Scarves General can't block.", "Huang Zhong, Shu General can't be blocked by more than one creature.", 'If target opponent has more cards in hand than you, draw cards equal to the difference.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Look at the top three cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", 'Other creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Other green creatures you control get +1/+1.', "Plainswalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Plains.)", 'Put target card from your graveyard on top of your library.', "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", "Red Cliffs Armada can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", "Return one or two target creatures to their owners' hands.", 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Return target sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Rockslide Ambush deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', 'Rolling Earthquake deals X damage to each creature without horsemanship and each player.', 'Sacrifice Fire Bowman: It deals 1 damage to any target. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', 'Sacrifice Loyal Retainers: Return target legendary creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', 'Search your library for a Forest card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a Plains, Island, Swamp, Mountain, or Forest card and put that card onto the battlefield. Then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top. You lose 2 life.', "Sima Yi, Wei Field Marshal's power is equal to the number of Swamps you control.", "Stalking Tiger can't be blocked by more than one creature.", 'Stolen Grain deals 5 damage to target opponent or planeswalker. You gain 5 life.', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", 'Take an extra turn after this one.', "Take an extra turn after this one. At the beginning of that turn's end step, you lose the game.", "Taoist Mystic can't be blocked by creatures with horsemanship.", 'Tap any number of untapped creatures you control. You gain 4 life for each creature tapped this way.', 'Tap one or two target creatures without horsemanship.', "Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains horsemanship. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship. This effect lasts indefinitely.)", "Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains horsemanship until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", 'Target creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent chooses a creature they control. Destroy that creature.', "Target opponent chooses a creature they control. Other creatures they control can't block this turn.", 'Target opponent discards two cards.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target opponent skips all combat phases of their next turn.', 'Untap all creatures that attacked this turn. After this main phase, there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase.', 'Vigilance', "Vigilance; horsemanship (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with horsemanship.)", 'When Corrupt Court Official enters the battlefield, target opponent discards a card.', 'When Corrupt Eunuchs enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to target creature.', 'When Council of Advisors enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Dong Zhou, the Tyrant enters the battlefield, target creature an opponent controls deals damage equal to its power to that player.', 'When Imperial Recruiter enters the battlefield, search your library for a creature card with power 2 or less, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Ravaging Horde enters the battlefield, destroy target land.', 'When Shu Grain Caravan enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.', 'When Shu Soldier-Farmers enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.', 'When Wei Assassins enters the battlefield, target opponent chooses a creature they control. Destroy that creature.', "When Wu Spy enters the battlefield, look at the top two cards of target player's library. Put one of them into their graveyard.", 'When Zodiac Dragon is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you may return it to your hand.', 'Whenever Flanking Troops attacks, you may tap target creature.', 'Whenever Hunting Cheetah deals damage to an opponent, you may search your library for a Forest card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Whenever Shu Defender blocks, it gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Slashing Tiger becomes blocked, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Trained Cheetah becomes blocked, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Wei Ambush Force attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever Yuan Shao's Infantry attacks alone, Yuan Shao's Infantry can't be blocked this combat.", 'Whenever Zhang Liao, Hero of Hefei deals damage to an opponent, that opponent discards a card.', 'Wu Admiral gets +1/+1 as long as an opponent controls an Island.', "Wu Warship can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", "Yellow Scarves Troops can't block.", 'You destroy four lands you control, then target opponent destroys four lands they control. Then Burning of Xinye deals 4 damage to each creature.', 'You draw three cards and you lose 3 life.', 'You gain 2 life for each creature you control.', 'You gain 8 life.', "You may have Lone Wolf assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "You may have Wolf Pack assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", "Young Wei Recruits can't block.", "Zhou Yu, Chief Commander can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", "{T}: Destroy target creature of your choice, then destroy target creature of an opponent's choice. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.", '{T}: Destroy target tapped nonblack creature. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: Draw a card. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', "{T}: Kongming's Contraptions deals 2 damage to target attacking creature. Activate only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.", '{T}: Put target creature card from your graveyard on top of your library. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', "{T}: Return Lady Sun and another target creature to their owners' hands. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.", "{T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.", '{T}: Target creature gets +0/+2 until end of turn. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: Target creature you control gets +2/+0 until end of turn. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: Target opponent discards a card. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: Target opponent discards two cards. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: Wu Longbowman deals 1 damage to any target. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: You gain 1 life. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.']
flavor: ['" . . . Cao Pi, Cao Rui, Fang, Mao, and briefly, Huan— / The Sima took the empire in their turn. . . ."', '". . . \'First take Jingzhou, next the Riverlands; / On that rich region, base your own royal stand.\' . . ."', '". . . But the time of Han had run—could he [Kongming] not tell?— / That night his master star fell past the hills. . . ."', '". . . By six offensives from the hills of Qi Kongming sought to change Han\'s destiny. . . ."', '". . . Cao\'s abdication changed the face of all; / No mighty battles marked the Southland\'s fall. . . ."', '". . . It was Pang Tong\'s boat-connecting scheme That let Zhou Yu accomplish his great deed."', '". . . Jiang Wei alone still strove with might and main: / Nine times more he fought the north—in vain. . . ."', '". . . Near death in Baidi, having reigned three years, / Bei sadly placed his son in Kongming\'s care. . . ."', '". . . The kingdoms three are now the stuff of dream, / For men to ponder, past all praise or blame."', '". . . The world\'s affairs rush on, an endless stream; / A sky-told fate, infinite in reach, dooms all. . . ."', '". . . Three kings no more—Chenliu, Guiming, Anle. / The fiefs and posts must now be filled anew. . . ."', '". . . Zhong Hui and Deng Ai next led armies west: / And to the Cao, Han\'s hills and streams now passed. . . ."', '"A man, and such a fool! I, a woman, will fight them for you."\\n—Lady Zhurong to her husband Meng Huo, before leading an army against the Shu', '"A splendid talent, admired of all men! His folly lay in serving Cao Cao\'s power."', '"Across the land rebellions seethed and swarmed / As vicious war lords swooped down on all sides."', '"After making me, Zhou Yu, did you have to make Kongming?"\\n—Zhou Yu crying to heaven on his deathbed', '"All men have their appointed time; that\'s something no horse can change."\\n—Liu Bei, after being told that the Dilu brings its master ill fortune', '"All warfare is based on deception."\\n—Sun Tzu, *Art of War* (trans. Giles)', '"Barbarian tribes with their rulers are inferior to Chinese states without them."\\n—Confucius, *The Analects* (trans. Lau)', '"But it was a year of dearth. People were reduced to eating leaves of jujube trees. Corpses were seen everywhere in the countryside."', '"Dong Zhuo\'s man, Lu Bu, warrior without peer, / Far surpassed the champions of his sphere."', '"He [Guan Yu] covered the ground on a thousand-*li* horse; / With dragon blade he took each pass by force."', '"If Heaven has placed it in your hands, it means that the throne is destined to be yours."', '"If I fail, my head is yours."\\n—Warrior\'s oath common during the Three Kingdoms period', '"In raiding and plundering, be like fire, in immovability like a mountain."\\n—Sun Tzu, *Art of War* (trans. Giles)', '"Leadership, not numbers, determines victory."\\n—A Wu commander, before his 5,000 troops forced 15,000 Wei troops to retreat from Ruxu', '"Lieutenants dishonored, corpses carted home; The general raises troops again to take revenge."', '"One score and four he reigned, the Southland king: / A dragon coiled, a tiger poised below the mighty Yangtze."', '"Only wisdom and virtue can truly win men\'s devotion."\\n—Liu Bei', '"Plans evolved within the tent decide a victory 1,000 *li* away."', '"Power-hungry eunuchs, the curse of the dynasty, have thrown the masses of the people into the depths of misery."', '"Spreading flames illumined cloud and sea: Cao Cao went down; \'twas Zhou Yu\'s victory."', '"Such a lord as this—all virtues\' height— Had never been, nor ever was again."', '"Swallowing his eye, the valiant Xiahou Dun fought on; / But Cao Cao\'s vanguard, its commander wounded, could not hold out for long."', '"The common folk are ceaselessly active. The fields are fertile and the soil productive, and neither flood nor drought plagues us."\\n—A Shu diplomat', '"The empire belongs to no one man but to all in the empire. He who has virtue shall possess it."', '"The empire, long united, must divide, and long divided, must unite."', '"Thorn bushes spring up wherever the army has passed. Lean years follow in the wake of a great war."\\n—Lao Tzu, *Tao Te Ching* (trans. Feng and English)', '"Those who know do not talk. Those who talk do not know."\\n—Lao Tzu, *Tao Te Ching*\\n(trans. Feng and English)', '"Thrice Xuande\'s ardent quest led to Nanyang, / Where Sleeping Dragon unveiled Han\'s partition: . . ."', '"To send the common people to war untrained is to throw them away."\\n—Confucius, *The Analects* (trans. Lau)', '"Trying to meet a worthy man in the wrong way is as bad as closing the door on an invited guest."\\n—Mencius, a Chinese philosopher', '"Unless you enter the tiger\'s lair, you cannot get hold of the tiger\'s cubs."\\n—Sun Tzu, *Art of War* (trans. Giles)', '"Until I\'ve gnawed their flesh and exterminated their clans, my humiliation will not be effaced."\\n—Liu Bei, on the death of his oath-brother Guan Yu', '"Virile in war, he kept the north in fear; His prodigies subdued the western sphere."', '"We three, though of separate ancestry, join in brotherhood . . . . We dare not hope to be together always but hereby vow to die the selfsame day."\\n—Peach Garden Oath', '"When you give offense to heaven, to whom can you pray?"\\n—Cao Cao, quoting Confucius', '"With fire he broke the battle at Bowang . . . . Striking fear deep into Cao Cao\'s soul, thus Kongming scored a coup at his debut."', '"[King Mulu\'s cheetahs] came riding on the winds, charging, with fangs bared and claws flexed."', "A cunning strategist, Cao Ren tricked Zhou Yu by letting him enter Nanjun. Zhou Yu thought he was capturing the city until Cao Ren's arrows rained down upon him.", 'After making the Peach Garden Oath, the three brothers raised an army of 500 youths to fight the Yellow Scarves rebellion.', 'As the Wu chief commander, Lu Meng conquered Shu-held Jingzhou in 219 by disguising soldiers as merchants on boats filled with hiding troops.', 'At Red Cliffs, Kongming and Zhou Yu each wrote his plan for defeating the Wei on the palm of his hand. They laughed as they both revealed the same word, "Fire."', "At the battle of Chang'an, Ma Chao defeated the two generals Cao Cao sent to guard the pass but was forced to flee when Cao Cao's trickery turned his own ally against him.", 'At the battle of Guandu, Cao Cao defeated Yuan Shao by raiding his grain depot, leaving him with no way to feed his troops.', "At the second battle of Ruxu, the brave Wu general Gan Ning raided Cao Cao's camp of 400,000 men with only 100 cavalry. Not a single man or horse was lost.", 'Bathing in this spring could cure ailments of body and mind alike.', "Before the battle of Red Cliffs, a supposedly sleeping Zhou Yu allowed his old friend, a Wei advisor, to steal a planted letter forged as if from Wei's two best admirals.", 'Believing they wrote the forged letter that had been stolen from Zhou Yu, Cao Cao rashly executed his two best admirals for treason.', 'Both Wu and Wei warships patrolled the Yangtze River, the natural border between the two kingdoms.', 'By appearing in places miles apart at the same time, Zuo Ci exhibited the mystic\'s ability to "shrink the land."', 'By the battle of Red Cliffs in the year 208, the Wu kingdom controlled more than 7,000 warships on the Yangtze.', 'By the year 208, Cao Cao commanded more than 1,000 experienced generals and a million infantry, cavalry, and naval troops.', 'Cao Cao was haunted to death by the ghosts of the empresses and other high courtiers he had murdered.', 'Cao Cao was more concerned with capabilities than lineage. He excelled at recruiting and retaining men of talent to serve him.', "Cao Cao's cousin, Cao Ren was known throughout the three kingdoms as the fiercest of warriors.", 'Confronting Cao Cao\'s army at Steepslope Bridge, Zhang Fei bellowed, "I am Zhang Fei of Yan! Who dares fight me to the death?" Cao Cao\'s army cowered and fled.', "During Kongming's campaigns against the Wei, his Shu troops rotated from the battlefront to the fields every hundred days.", 'Fish and bear paws—one can\'t have both.\\n—Chinese idiom meaning "you can\'t have it both ways"', "Following the battle of Redcliffs, both Liu Bei and Sun Quan coveted the province of Jingzhou. After Sun Quan's troops failed to capture it, Liu Bei's succeeded.", "Frustrated with Cao Cao's control of the imperial court, Emperor Xian secretly issued an edict condemning him, using his own blood as ink.", 'He will win who, prepared himself, waits to take the enemy unprepared."\\n—Sun Tzu, *Art of War* (trans. Giles)', 'In ancient China, not wearing armor could be a fatal mistake. Guan Yu, Zhou Yu, Sun Ce, and other heros were struck by poison arrows.', "In establishing the Shu kingdom, Liu Bei's forces fought against Ma Chao at Chengdu. Eventually, Ma Chao surrendered and became one of Liu Bei's Tiger Generals.", "Incensed by their opponents' unrelenting taunts, even wise generals were known to rashly lead their troops into battle—often to disastrous defeats.", 'Keeping a million-man army fed was no easy task. Grain and rice caravans were the lifeblood of the empire.', 'Kongming and Lu Su tricked Wei troops into shooting over 100,000 arrows at them to later use against the Wei at Red Cliffs.', "Kongming's first campaign against the Wei kingdom was a rousing success until an arrogant Shu general, Ma Su, foolishly lost the city of Jieting.", 'Kongming\'s predecessor helped Liu Bei win the battle of Fancheng by recognizing and defeating Cao Ren\'s use of the dreaded "Eight Gold Locks" formation.', "Liu Bei lost many men at the battle of Runan because of his lack of strategy. It wasn't until he met Kongming that he began to truly succeed as a leader.", "Lu Su served as an intermediary between the Wu and Shu kingdoms until Zhou Yu's death in 210, when he became Wu's supreme commander.", "Named for the eastern part of the sky, the source of energy and renewal, Guan Yu's crescent-moon blade weighed over 100 pounds.", 'One of the greatest steeds in the empire, Red Hare could travel a thousand *li* a day and climb hills as if running on flat ground.', 'Only twenty years after the Sima clan united the empire, invading barbarians divided it again.', 'Out of time and options, Kongming was forced to bluff at Xicheng. He tricked an army of 150,000 Wei by leaving the city gates open and calmly playing the zither.', 'Over 500,000 commoners followed Zhang Jue, General of Heaven, in his attempt to overthrow the corrupt Han dynasty.', 'Penniless and far from home, many former Yellow Scarves and other soldiers became bandits to survive.', 'Sima Yi fought for four generations of the Cao family before his own grandson became emperor and united the three kingdoms.', 'Sister to Sun Quan and wife to Liu Bei, Lady Sun often felt her loyalty to both tested.', 'Soldiers often blocked off the steep mountain passes to ambush enemy troops in western and central China.', 'Starving and worn, Cao Cao escaped from the battle of Red Cliffs with only 27 of his original 800,000 men.', "Sun Quan's long and successful rule in the years 199 to 251 was due to his ability to choose and foster talented advisors and generals.", 'Taking control of powerful court positions one by one, eunuchs eventually brought on the fall of the Han dynasty, leading to the chaos of the Three Kingdoms.', 'Taoists chose to be hermits for many reasons, but all shared one unchanging goal: to follow the Tao.', "The Wu kingdom's well-trained admirals were integral to the Southlands' victory at Red Cliffs as well as the kingdom's defense.", 'The battle of Puyang marked the beginning of the end for Lu Bu. He lost the city—and later his life—to Cao Cao.', "The first battle of Hefei was Sun Quan's last as a field general. From then on he let his generals command in the field while he directed battle from behind the front lines.", 'The mourning families of commanders and generals were often given land, valuables, or money to compensate for their losses.', 'The overnight appearance of miles of "armed" Wu forts at Guangling frightened a much vaster Wei force into fleeing for their lives.', 'The province of Jingzhou was the fulcrum of the three kingdoms. At separate times it was coveted and controlled by the Wu, the Shu, and the Wei.', 'The stubborn Meng Huo was captured and released by Kongming seven times before finally surrendering.', "Though he held the title of prime minister, Cao Cao used the emperor's name to exert his own influence on the empire.", 'Through his allies, Meng Huo commanded several hundred thousand troops composed of cavalry, rattan-armored warriors, infantry, naked men with swords, and wild animals.', 'Throughout Chinese history, generals have often been referred to as tigers for their fierceness, strength, and bravery.', 'Throughout the three kingdoms, important generals were often guarded by small groups of expert soldiers known as "elite companions."', 'To taunt a man into action, call him a coward. To insult him beyond forgiveness, call him a jackal.', 'Trip wire, hooked poles, and sunken pits were commonly used to unhorse riders during the Three Kingdoms period.', 'Upon his return to the capitol after taking soldiers to loot a nearby peaceful town, the prime minister, Dong Zhou, boasted of it as a victory over bandits.', 'Using nature to their advantage, wise Three Kingdoms generals often let dammed rivers loose to destroy their enemies.', 'Wei won the battle of Hefei when Zhang Liao defeated Sun Quan and then foiled a Wu scheme to incite rebellion.', "When Zhuge Jin proposed the marriage of Guan Yu's daugher and Sun Quan's heir, Guan Yu's arrogant refusal led to disaster.", "While defending their southern borders, both the Wu and Shu kingdoms fought against the barbarians' trained elephants.", "While pursuing the remnants of Yuan Shao's forces into the Wuhan Desert, Cao Cao was temporarily turned back by a fierce sandstorm.", 'With only 70,000 men under his command at the battle of Guandu, Cao Cao was able to defeat Yuan Shao and his 700,000.', "Zhang Fei's uncharacteristic alliance with a defeated Riverlands general, Yan Yan, allowed Shu forces to advance through forty-five Riverlands strongpoints with no casualties.", 'Zhang Jue, leader of the Yellow Scarves rebellion, was a Taoist master and tutored his soldiers in those arts.', "Zhao Zilong was a brave and noble warrior. Twice he rescued Liu Bei's son, Liu Shan.", 'Zhou Yu, Sun Ce, and other famous generals feigned their deaths in order to later surprise their opponents.']
artist: ['Ai Desheng', 'Cai Tingting', 'Chen Weidong', 'Ding Songjian', 'Fang Yue', 'Gao Jianzhang', 'Gao Yan', 'He Jiancheng', 'Hong Yan', 'Huang Qishi', 'Inoue Junichi', 'Jack Wei', 'Ji Yong', 'Jiaming', 'Jiang Zhuqing', 'Junko Taguchi', 'Kang Yu', 'Koji', 'Ku Xueming', 'Kuang Sheng', 'LHQ', 'Li Tie', 'Li Wang', 'Li Xiaohua', 'Li Youliang', 'Li Yousong', 'Lin Yan', 'Liu Jianjian', 'Liu Shangying', 'Miao Aili', 'Mitsuaki Sagiri', 'Qi Baocheng', 'Qiao Dafu', 'Qin Jun', 'Qu Xin', 'Quan Xuejun', 'Shang Huitong', 'Solomon Au Yeung', 'Song Shikai', 'Sun Nan', 'Tang Xiaogu', 'Wang Chuxiong', 'Wang Feng', 'Wang Yuqun', 'Xu Tan', 'Xu Xiaoming', 'Yang Guangmai', 'Yang Hong', 'Yang Jun Kwon', 'Zhang Jiazhen', 'Zhao Tan']
